# Only for the tests.
LOG_LEVEL=silent
WEBHOOK_SECRET=test-secret-0123456789abcdef-0123456789
# The tests' database, on your own computer. The tests empty it and fill it again every time: it
# has to be a different one, never the real one. If DATABASE_URL is already in the environment (in
# CI, for example), Node doesn't replace it with this one.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://shop:shop@localhost:5432/shop_test
# The practice identity provider (npm run provider). The tests in oauth.test.ts start their own,
# on a free port, and change OIDC_ISSUER.
OIDC_ISSUER=http://localhost:9000
OIDC_CLIENT_ID=shop
OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=test-provider-secret-0123456789abcdef
OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/v2/session/provider/callback
# The sites requests with the session cookie are accepted from (lesson 7).
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
# Redis, for the tests of the limits' store (redis-store.test.ts) and of the queue: database 1, not
# 0, which is the shop's. The cache's (cache.test.ts) use 2 of the same Redis. Without this line,
# those tests are skipped; CI sets it.
# REDIS_URL_TESTS=redis://localhost:6379/1
# The responses of /v2 are checked against the contract (src/contract-responses.ts): one that
# doesn't meet it is a 500, so every test, besides its own job, is a contract test.
VALIDATE_RESPONSES=fail
